From 0866136e8ed145dec31942b1b5663c63d0e64350 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:32:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AI Chatbot step, Limit, API key connections: import n8n
 "Willow 4.0" completely

- New AI Chatbot node (ai.chatbot): instructions, conversation memory per contact
  (workflowChatMemory, per workflow, 90-day TTL), Google Sheets look-ups the AI can
  search (only matching rows go to the AI). Works with OpenAI, Claude and Gemini.
- New Limit node (logic.limit).
- New "API key / token" connection; HTTP Request "Sign in with" sends it only to the
  websites listed on the connection. New Body "Fields" type builds safe JSON.
- n8n import: AI Agent + chat model + memory + Sheets tools become one AI Chatbot step;
  Limit; header auth; executeOnce hint; $now.format('yyyy-MM-dd') -> $today.
  willow.json now imports with 0 "Needs replacing" steps.
- Form field types "credential" and "list"; connection fields inside a step are
  permission-checked on save, re-linked on import and included in exports.
- Vercel without Redis: webhook calls stay open until the run ends (WEBHOOK_WAIT_SECONDS).
- Firebase nodes can no longer reach the platform's AI collections in its own project.
- Template "AI: live chat guest assistant (GoHighLevel)". 13 new tests (240 pass).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Way2MShq9L17Ca2pfhv9Yv
